Emily: quick heads-up — I'm landing a PR for the troubleshooting guide on 429s/timeouts. there's a confusing bit about concurrent requests vs per-client rate windows that keeps tripping up customers.
Aj: can you point to the paragraph? i skimmed but didn't catch the exact wording.
Emily: second paragraph under 'Why 429s happen' — it says 'too many open connections' which is vague. we should call out "concurrent inflight requests" vs "rate per minute" and show a tiny example for node + python SDKs.
Samir: agreed. also add an explicit note about idempotency keys for write operations — folks retrying can cause duplicate side effects.
Kevin: i can draft a short JS snippet for exponential backoff + trimming the prompt when you're near the context window. small, copy-paste ready.
Emily: perfect — we want both a backoff snippet and a context-trim helper. keep the JS snippet using the new SDK pattern (client.request + signal) so it matches other docs.
Aj: here's a draft i used in a support ticket, feel free to polish:

```
// JS exponential backoff + context-trim pseudo
async function callWithBackoff(client, req, maxRetries=4) {
  let attempt = 0;
  while (true) {
    try {
      return await client.generate(req);
    } catch (err) {
      if (!isRetryable(err) || attempt >= maxRetries) throw err;
      const backoff = Math.pow(2, attempt) * 250 + Math.random() * 100;
      // if error indicates context limit, try trimming:
      if (err.code === 'context_length_exceeded') req.prompt = trimPrompt(req.prompt, 0.2);
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
      attempt++;
    }
  }
}
```

Emily: nice. we'll want a Python snippet too and a one-sentence explanation: "Prefer idempotency keys for non-idempotent ops; prefer client-side batching or concurrency limits to avoid 429s; use context trimming only when response fidelity can be reduced."
Samir: also add an ops note: when customers see repeated 429 spikes, check prefix caching and continuous-batching config — a bad cache miss storm looks like a traffic surge.
Kevin: small nit — change the JS example to call `client.chat.completions.create` (matches SDK phrasing) and include signal cancellation example for timeouts.
Emily: good call. i'll update the PR with both snippets and link to the SDK retries section. can someone review the wording for clarity? cc @Aj @Samir
Aj: i'll review after standup.
DocsBot: PR #4521 opened by Emily — docs/429-concurrency-clarify — reviewers: Aj, Samir, Kevin :partyparrot:
Emily: thanks. i'll also add a short migration note for teams on Dedicated: "if you have many small clients, set a per-client concurrency limiter (eg 5 inflight) rather than relying on server-side burst capacity".
Samir: add a pointer to the console trace tab so they can correlate high inflight counts with tail-latency.
Emily: done in the draft. one last thing — let's add a gloss for error codes we return: `rate_exceeded`, `requests_per_minute`, `context_length_exceeded`, `concurrent_limit`. a short table inline will help.
Kevin: ok i'll add that table and a final proofread.
Emily: awesome — landing later today unless anyone objects. thx everyone :shipit:
